\vspace{0.5cm}

A compound proposition is called \textbf{satisfiable} if there exists at least one
truth-value assignment that makes it \textbf{true}.

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{primaryblue}{\textbf{\faInfoCircle\ Key Points:}}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em]
    \item Every \textbf{tautology} is satisfiable (it is true under all assignments).
    \item Every \textbf{contingency} is satisfiable (it is true under some assignments).
    \item A \textbf{contradiction} is the only type that is \textbf{not satisfiable}.
    \item Satisfiability is a central concept in computer science (the SAT problem).
\end{itemize}

