We convert the conditional to disjunction form and simplify algebraically.

\vspace{0.3cm}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|}
\hline
\rowcolor{primaryblue!20}
\textbf{Expression} & \textbf{Law Applied} \\
\hline
$\neg(p \rightarrow q) \rightarrow \neg q$ & Given \\
\hline
$\neg(p \rightarrow q) \rightarrow \neg q$ & (rewrite conditional) \\
\hline
$\neg[\neg(p \rightarrow q)] \lor \neg q$ & $A \rightarrow B \equiv \neg A \lor B$ \\
\hline
$(p \rightarrow q) \lor \neg q$ & Double Negation Law \\
\hline
$(\neg p \lor q) \lor \neg q$ & $p \rightarrow q \equiv \neg p \lor q$ \\
\hline
$\neg p \lor (q \lor \neg q)$ & Associative Law \\
\hline
$\neg p \lor \mathbf{T}$ & Negation Law: $q \lor \neg q \equiv \mathbf{T}$ \\
